WEBVTT


00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:07.430
My new to me, Toyota K S 858
arrived in mint condition.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:12.050
It had been stored for quite some time,
but everything was there and it was

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.010
spotless.

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:18.860
Now, I expected the sponge bar to be flat,
but I didn't expect to find rust on the

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:19.370
needles.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.850
There was no rust anywhere
else in the machine.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.880
Apparently the sponge absorbed and held
moisture against the needles causing the

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.330
rust.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.330
So why is this a problem?

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:35.449
Imagine forming stitches with yarn.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.480
The rust prevents the yarn from slipping
smoothly along the shank of the needle and

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.920
forming this ditch properly.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.030
I carefully removed each
needle from the needle bed.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.290
Be sure to close the latch as you
slip the needle out of the channel.

00:00:55.019 --> 00:00:59.699
On this machine, you really need to bend
the needle slightly to get it up and over

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:00.720
the back of the bed.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.430
But don't worry.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.910
These needles are designed to be used
with the lace carriage, so they're pretty

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:06.630
flexible.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.479
Don't force them, but they
will bend enough to remove.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.690
I soaked all of the needles in a jar,
partially filled with denatured alcohol,

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.900
and this removed most
of the rust by itself.

00:01:21.775 --> 00:01:26.785
For those really stubborn spots, a bit
of fine sand paper or Emory cloth did the

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:27.175
trick.

00:01:28.695 --> 00:01:31.815
This really took some
time, but it's so worth it.

00:01:32.465 --> 00:01:38.465
After replacing the sponge bar, I now have
a practically mint machine to play with.

